    "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. Toxicity Metric Issue (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n**Problem**: The `runEvaluations` function passes both outputs and references to all metrics. The `toxicityMetric` function interprets its second parameter as `bannedTerms`, so when references were passed, they were treated as keywords to flag (causing \"hello\" in the output to be incorrectly flagged as toxic).\n\n**Fix**: Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in `DEFAULT_METRICS` to only pass outputs, not references:\n```javascript\n(outs) => toxicityMetric(outs)\n```\n\nThis ensures the function only receives what it needs when used in the default metrics pipeline, while preserving backwards compatibility for direct calls with custom bannedTerms.\n\n### 2. Governance Exports Issue (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n**Problem**: Constants like `APPROVAL_STATUSES` were imported from schema.js but only exported as part of the default export, not as named exports. The test needed to import them as named exports.\n\n**Fix**: Added named export statements for all the constants:\n```javascript\nexport {\n  APPROVAL_STATUSES,\n  DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS,\n  GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS,\n  RISK_LEVELS\n};\n```\n\n## Results\n- \u2705 All 28 tests passing (8 test files)\n- \u2705 All public exports preserved\n- \u2705 No test files modified\n- \u2705 Source code fixed, not tests",
